  "id": "Compound::DB00262 - Disease::DOID:2531",
  "verbalization": "Carmustine's potential role in treating hematologic cancer is supported by its ability to cause dysplasia, cerebral hematoma, and idiopathic pneumonia syndrome, all of which are linked to hematologic malignancies. These effects are mediated through a common pathway involving antineoplastic agents and organochlorine compounds. The evidence suggests that Carmustine may exert its therapeutic effect by inducing cellular dysplasia or inflammation, which can lead to the progression or suppression of hematologic cancer. The shared ancestry of Carmustine with other antineoplastic agents and organochlorine compounds highlights a potential mechanism of action that involves systemic effects on cellular processes. While the exact mechanism remains unclear, the integration of these pathways underscores Carmustine's potential as a repurposed agent for hematologic cancer treatment.",
